  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 90\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-59 \\\\ 118 \\\\ -33\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -10 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 180\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vector lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$",
